# npm Supply-Chain Hardening

- Commit and use lockfiles; install with frozen lockfile in CI.
- Prefer pinned/exact versions for security-sensitive deps; review sudden major bumps.
- Run `npm audit` / equivalent; triage high/critical before merge.
- Avoid unnecessary lifecycle scripts; be wary of new packages with postinstall exfil patterns.
- Minimize dependency surface; prefer well-maintained packages with clear ownership.
- Do not commit `.npmrc` tokens; use CI secrets / `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN` injection.
- After adding deps, skim publish time, maintainer changes, and download anomalies for brand-new packages.
